.TH CELLBOOT 1 "2026-10-15" "CellBoot v0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cellboot \- AcreetionOS's overwrite-immune Windows boot lane (KVM-guest launcher)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cellboot
[will be a real command at
.BR milestone/M0.6-cellbootctl.md ;
today only the repo scaffold exists]
.SH DESCRIPTION
CellBoot boots Windows WITHOUT fighting Windows Update.
\&\fB\EFI\cellboot\fR is a path Windows Update never learns about: the host
EFI chain is entirely AcreetionOS-owned. CellBoot boots a minimal Linux
KVM host and launches the \fBuser's own official, unmodified\fR Windows boot
files as a KVM guest. Windows validates its own Secure Boot chain inside
the guest; it cannot overwrite the host chain and cannot reset NVRAM to
steal the boot.
.sp
VaultBoot, the guest boot lane, ships NO Windows; the user brings their own
copy from Microsoft and owns license compliance (see README).
